      "message": "[error] Line 106: 🔴 `take(1)` does not actually guarantee completion here because `registeredName(forAddress:)` only emits on `.found`. For `.notFound`/`.error`, this subscription stays alive indefinitely, so repeated `lookupName(...)` calls for unresolved participants still accumulate disposables/observers over time. This recreates the long-session growth issue in a narrower form. Fix by making the lookup stream emit a terminal value for negative outcomes (e.g., `String?` or a result enum) so `take(1)` can complete, or by ensuring only one in-flight subscription exists per participant/address and disposing/replacing it explicitly.",
